course: dictionary
lesson: 8277
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one the writer means. Ring is a good example. It can be a round band, a circle, a sound a bell makes, or a phone call. «A boy in New York had ringing in his ears that would not go away.» Here ringing is a sound, because ears can hear sounds, and a sound is what keeps ringing on.
explain: «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? A round band or loop fits, so ring means a round band here. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «When the bell rings she stops at once and lines up.» A bell that rings makes a sound. The same word can be a circle in another sentence, so always check the clues around it before you decide.
fact: Ring can be a noun (a thing, such as a ring) or a verb (an action, such as to ring).
fact: «Ring» means a round band, like one worn on a finger.
fact: «Ring» can also mean a circle shape, such as the rings of a tree or the rings on the Olympic flag.
fact: «To ring» means to make a bell sound, and «to ring someone» (UK) means to phone them.
fact: «To ring» something means to draw a circle around it, and the past tense is «ringed».
exercise: «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» What is a ring here? | A bell sound | A phone call | A place for boxing | *A round band or loop
exercise: «When the bell rings, she stops at once and lines up.» What does rings mean here? | *Makes a bell sound | A round band | To draw a circle around something | To phone someone
exercise: «A boy in New York had ringing in his ears that would not go away.» What does ringing mean here? | A round band worn on a finger | A circle shape | A place for boxing | *A sound, like a bell
test:  Tom says, «I will ring you tonight.» What does ring mean? | To draw a circle around something | *To phone someone | A round band | A circle shape
test:  In a story, a girl finds a magic ring. What does ring mean here? | To make a bell sound | A place for boxing | *A round band, like one worn on a finger | A tree's age
exam: Which sentence uses ring to mean to draw a circle around something? | The boxers stepped into the ring | The school bell rang at break time | Their phone rang twice last night | *She ringed the wrong answer in red pen
